-- Imported from Blawx by `l4 blawx --import` (BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R14, §10 P5).
--
--   source        beard_tax.yaml
--   ruledoc       "Beard Tax Act"
--   rows          4 blawx.workspace, 1 blawx.blawxtest
--   blocks        62 across 13 block types
--   WARNING       stored `scasp_encoding` is STALE against the current
--                 generator (P5-2) in 3 row(s), first sec_1_section.
--                 The XML is canonical (R14); the encodings were not used.
--
-- Blawx models a flat universe of atoms under predicates of one, two or
-- more places: a category is `c(X)`, a category-valued attribute is
-- `a(X,Y)`, a relationship is `r(X,Y,Z)`. So this lift declares ONE record
-- for the universe, carrying one input slot per declared predicate (the
-- s(CASP) fact channel: `MAYBE BOOLEAN` at one place, a list of argument
-- tuples above it) and one BOOLEAN decision per predicate. The defeat layer
-- is unfolded: one decision per (section, literal) pair, named from the
-- generator's own #pred wording.
--
-- A value-typed attribute is a partial FUNCTION, not a predicate: it gets a
-- field of its own sort instead of a `<p> fact` channel, a `p x` decision
-- saying the attribute is DEFINED, and a `the p of x` reader for the VALUE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `negation-as-failure`

§ `Beard Tax Act`

§§ `Ontology`

-- @ref sec_1_section new_category_declaration person  (NLG "" / "is a person")
-- @ref sec_1_section new_attribute_declaration person.bearded : boolean
-- @ref sec_1_section new_attribute_declaration person.facial_hair_length_mm : number
-- @ref sec_1__para_a_section new_attribute_declaration person.facial_hair_on_chin : boolean
-- @ref sec_1__para_a_section new_attribute_declaration person.facial_hair_below_chin : boolean
-- @ref sec_1__para_a_section new_attribute_declaration person.qualifies_s1a : boolean
-- @ref sec_1__para_b_section new_attribute_declaration person.facial_hair_continuous : boolean
-- @ref sec_1__para_b_section new_attribute_declaration person.qualifies_s1b : boolean
DECLARE Object
    HAS
      @desc the object's Blawx atom
      name                            IS A STRING
      @desc x is a person
      `person fact`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      @desc x is bearded
      `bearded fact`                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      @desc x 's facial hair is on the chin
      `facial_hair_on_chin fact`      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      @desc x 's facial hair is below the chin
      `facial_hair_below_chin fact`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      @desc x qualifies under section 1 a
      `qualifies_s1a fact`            IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      @desc x 's facial hair is ear to ear below the nose
      `facial_hair_continuous fact`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      @desc x qualifies under section 1 b
      `qualifies_s1b fact`            IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      @desc x 's facial hair is v mm in length
      facial_hair_length_mm           IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref sec_1_section new_attribute_declaration person.facial_hair_length_mm : number
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE facial_hair_length_mm x @nlg there is a value v such that %x% 's facial hair is v mm in length
    IF isJust (x's facial_hair_length_mm)

-- the value itself, read under the definedness conjunct above.
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the facial_hair_length_mm of` x
    MEANS fromMaybe 0 (x's facial_hair_length_mm)

GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE person x @nlg %x% is a person
    IF holds (x's `person fact`)

GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE facial_hair_on_chin x @nlg %x% 's facial hair is on the chin
    IF holds (x's `facial_hair_on_chin fact`)

GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE facial_hair_below_chin x @nlg %x% 's facial hair is below the chin
    IF holds (x's `facial_hair_below_chin fact`)

GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE facial_hair_continuous x @nlg %x% 's facial hair is ear to ear below the nose
    IF holds (x's `facial_hair_continuous fact`)

§§ `BTA 1 — In this Act, beard means any facial hair no shorter than 5 millimetres in length that: (a) occurs on or below the chin, or (b) exists in an uninterrupted line from the front of one ear to the front of the other ear below the nose.`

@ref BTA 1 — sec_1_section attributed_rule (defeasible FALSE, inapplicable FALSE)
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `according to BTA 1, x is bearded (clause 1)` x
    IF  person x
    AND `the facial_hair_length_mm of` x AT LEAST 5
    AND facial_hair_length_mm x
    AND qualifies_s1a x

@ref BTA 1 — sec_1_section attributed_rule (defeasible FALSE, inapplicable FALSE)
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `according to BTA 1, x is bearded (clause 2)` x
    IF  person x
    AND `the facial_hair_length_mm of` x AT LEAST 5
    AND facial_hair_length_mm x
    AND qualifies_s1b x

-- `according_to(sec_1_section,bearded,X)` has 2 clauses in this section; their disjunction is the section's answer.
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `according to BTA 1, x is bearded` x
    IF `according to BTA 1, x is bearded (clause 1)` x
    OR `according to BTA 1, x is bearded (clause 2)` x

@ref BTA 1 — indefeasible: no `not blawx_defeated` conjunct
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conclusion in BTA 1 that x is bearded holds` x
    IF `according to BTA 1, x is bearded` x

@ref BTA 1 — sec_1__para_a_section attributed_rule (defeasible FALSE, inapplicable FALSE)
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 a (clause 1)` x IF facial_hair_on_chin x

@ref BTA 1 — sec_1__para_a_section attributed_rule (defeasible FALSE, inapplicable FALSE)
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 a (clause 2)` x IF facial_hair_below_chin x

-- `according_to(sec_1_section,qualifies_s1a,X)` has 2 clauses in this section; their disjunction is the section's answer.
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 a` x
    IF `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 a (clause 1)` x
    OR `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 a (clause 2)` x

@ref BTA 1 — indefeasible: no `not blawx_defeated` conjunct
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conclusion in BTA 1 that x qualifies under section 1 a holds` x
    IF `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 a` x

@ref BTA 1 — sec_1__para_b_section attributed_rule (defeasible FALSE, inapplicable FALSE)
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 b` x IF facial_hair_continuous x

@ref BTA 1 — indefeasible: no `not blawx_defeated` conjunct
GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conclusion in BTA 1 that x qualifies under section 1 b holds` x
    IF `according to BTA 1, x qualifies under section 1 b` x

§§ `The base predicates`

-- `p(x) :- holds(sec_N, p, x).` for every section concluding p, OR-joined,
-- plus the scenario fact channel (a bare `p(a).` is another clause of p).

GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE bearded x @nlg %x% is bearded
    IF holds (x's `bearded fact`)
    OR `the conclusion in BTA 1 that x is bearded holds` x

GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE qualifies_s1a x @nlg %x% qualifies under section 1 a
    IF holds (x's `qualifies_s1a fact`)
    OR `the conclusion in BTA 1 that x qualifies under section 1 a holds` x

GIVEN x IS AN Object
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE qualifies_s1b x @nlg %x% qualifies under section 1 b
    IF holds (x's `qualifies_s1b fact`)
    OR `the conclusion in BTA 1 that x qualifies under section 1 b holds` x

§§ `Tests`

-- blawxtest are_they_bearded — `?- bearded(Person).`
-- NOT LIFTED (blawx-lift/unbound-query-empty-universe): the query binds a free variable and the document declares no objects and asserts no ground facts, so there is nothing for an #EVAL to range over.
